-- name    : AlgebraicGeometry_RegularLocalRingFaithfullyFlatDescent
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @Claude
-- created : 2026-09-05T04:28:24.773853+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/184254ea-3b35-5109-98f7-b38745a26c03
-- title:
--   Descent of regularity along faithfully flat ring maps
-- statement:
--   The module studies when regularity of a local ring descends along a faithfully flat algebra map $A \to B$, and packages the general statement as a named proposition.
--
--   Two `Prop`-valued definitions carry the general claim. `RegularDescendsAlongFaithfullyFlat` asserts: for all commutative rings $A$ and $B$ with an $A$-algebra structure making $B$ a faithfully flat $A$-module, if $B$ is a regular local ring then so is $A$. `RegularDescendsAlongFlatLocalHom` asserts: for all $A$ local and Noetherian and all $A$-algebras $B$ that are flat as $A$-modules with $B$ regular local, if $\operatorname{algebraMap} A B$ is a local homomorphism then $A$ is regular local. The theorem `regularDescendsAlongFaithfullyFlat_iff_flatLocalHom` shows the two propositions are equivalent, in each fixed pair of universes.
--
--   The descent itself is proved unconditionally when the target is a Noetherian valuation domain. The supporting structure-descent lemmas say that, for $B$ faithfully flat over $A$: $A$ is Noetherian if $B$ is; $A$ is local if $B$ is; the structure map of two local rings is a local homomorphism; and $\dim A \le \dim B$ as Krull dimensions in $\mathrm{WithBot}\,\mathbb{N}^\infty$. In a valuation domain $B$, the ideal generated by the image of a nonempty finite subset $s \subseteq A$ is generated by the image of a single element of $s$; combined with $\operatorname{comap}\circ\operatorname{map} = \mathrm{id}$ for faithfully flat extensions this makes $\mathfrak{m}_A$ principal, whence $A$ is a regular local ring. Corollaries cover targets that are fields, discrete valuation domains, regular local rings of Krull dimension $0$ (such a ring is a field) and regular local domains of Krull dimension $\le 1$ (such a ring is a valuation ring), and the free-module variants. Instantiations at $(\mathbb{Q},\mathbb{Q})$ and $(\mathbb{Z}_p,\mathbb{Z}_p)$ are recorded. Finally, $\mathbb{Q}[\varepsilon]$ is shown not to be regular local, which refutes both descent along surjective local homomorphisms without flatness ($\mathbb{Q}[\varepsilon] \to \mathbb{Q}$) and ascent along faithfully flat maps ($\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{Q}[\varepsilon]$).
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** `IsRegularLocalRing`, `Module.FaithfullyFlat`, `ValuationRing` and `ringKrullDim` are Mathlib's; the two descent propositions `RegularDescendsAlongFaithfullyFlat` and `RegularDescendsAlongFlatLocalHom` are the project's own names for a statement Mathlib does not provide in general, and the theorems here establish it for Noetherian valuation-domain targets.
--
--   **Where it is used.** The descent lemmas are used where regularity of a ring has to be deduced from regularity of a faithfully flat (in practice finite flat) extension of it, as in passing between models at different levels in the theory of modular curves and Hecke algebras.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_AlgebraicGeometry_RegularLocalRingFaithfullyFlatDescent.lean

